  "description": "Architectural decisions are scattered across historical plans, commits, and PRs. This adds a local bootstrap that turns those sources into a Deciduous decision graph without writing directly into the accepted graph.\n\n## Changes\n- Add the scoped Deciduous configuration, record-store setup, and contributor instructions.\n- Preserve the historical planning triage and align the adoption plan with verified viewer behavior.\n- Build from pinned source snapshots, full git history, and merged PRs from the preceding 12 months plus older references.\n- Require validation and explicit digest-bound acceptance before promotion; restrict writes to graph records and the two public JSON exports.\n- Preserve the distinction between source-reported facts and the explicitly reviewed audit association.\n\n## Verification\n- `pnpm check` and `pnpm test` passed; all 18 test tasks succeeded.\n- Explicit-file strict TypeScript checks passed for the bootstrap implementation and tests.\n- Real CLI fixtures cover isolated snapshots, validation, acceptance, promotion, recovery, and signing-independent test repositories.\n- The final git-history timeout regression passed with all 86 tests in its integration-test file.\n\n## Scope\nNo full-history bootstrap or promotion into Sparkle's graph has been run. This does not publish the viewer, enable scheduled refresh, invoke a model, or add browser document reading. Those remain separate steps.",
